<!--
  Author: Kris Hollingsworth
  Class: Math122-Calculus 2
  Date: 7/23/26
  File: E02-C24-03-methods-for-trig-two.oml
  Description:
    Fully worked example of Trig Substitution
  Raw Link: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DoctorHaitch/doenet-math-problems/main/M122-Calculus-2/E02-C24-03-methods-for-trig-two.oml
-->
<setup>
  <mathList unordered name="cos_double_angle_forms">
    <m>\cos^{2}\left(x\right)-\sin^{2}\left(x\right)</m>
    <m>1-2\sin^{2}\left(x\right)</m> <m>2\cos^{2}\left(x\right)-1</m>
  </mathList>
</setup>
<cascade>
  <div>
    <p>
      The basic trigonometric double angle identities are
      <mathInput name="sin_double_angle" forAnswer="$identities_one">
        <label><m>\sin(2\cdot x) =</m></label>
      </mathInput><text hide="not($identities_one.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text> and
      <mathInput name="cos_double_angle" forAnswer="$identities_one">
        <label><m>\cos(2\cdot x) =</m></label>
      </mathInput><text hide="not($identities_one.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer
        name="identities_one"
        numAwardsCredited="2"
        hide="$identities_one.creditAchieved=1"
      >
        <award credit=".5">
          <when>
            $sin_double_angle=<m>2\sin\left(x\right)\cos\left(x\right)</m>
          </when>
        </award>
        <award credit=".5">
          <when>
            $cos_double_angle=<m>
              \cos^{2}\left(x\right)-\sin^{2}\left(x\right)
            </m>
            or $cos_double_angle=<m>1-2\sin^{2}\left(x\right)</m> or
            $cos_double_angle=<m>2\cos^{2}\left(x\right)-1</m>
          </when>
        </award>
      </answer>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>
      <choiceInput inline name="trig_choice_one" shuffleOrder>
        <label>The identity </label>
        <choice><m>\sin(2\cdot x)</m></choice>
        <choice name="correct_one"><m>\cos(2\cdot x)</m></choice>
      </choiceInput>
      <text hide="not($identities_two.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
      <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="trig_choice_two">
        <label>can be
      rewritten quickly into several other highly useful forms using the</label>
        <choice name="correct_two">
          Pythagorean identity <m>\sin^2(x)+\cos^2(x)=1</m>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          sum of angles identity
          <m>\sin(x+y) = \sin(x)\cos(y)+\sin(y)\cos(x)</m>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          sum of angles identity
          <m>\cos(x+y) = \cos(x)\cos(y)-\sin(x)\sin(y)</m>
        </choice>
        <choice>shift identity <m>\sin(x+\frac{\pi}{2}) = \cos(x)</m></choice>
      </choiceInput><text hide="not($identities_two.creditAchieved=1)">
        ✅
      </text>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer
        name="identities_two"
        numAwardsCredited="2"
        hide="$identities_two.creditAchieved=1"
      >
        <award credit=".5"><when>$correct_one.selected</when></award>
        <award credit=".5"><when>$correct_two.selected</when></award>
      </answer>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>
      Then three equivalent forms of <m>\cos(2\cdot x)</m> are
      <ol>
        <li>
          <mathInput name="form_one" prefill="$cos_double_angle">
            <!-- prefillLatex="\cos^{2}\left(x\right)-\sin^{2}\left(x\right)" -->
            <shortDescription>
              Enter one form of cosine of 2x.
            </shortDescription>
          </mathInput><text hide="not($answer_forms.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
        </li>
        <li>
          <mathInput name="form_two"><!-- prefillLatex="1-2\sin^{2}\left(x\right)" -->
            <shortDescription>
              Enter another form of cosine of 2x.
            </shortDescription>
          </mathInput><text hide="not($answer_forms.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
        </li>
        <li>
          <mathInput name="form_three">
            <!-- prefillLatex="2\cos^{2}\left(x\right)-1" -->
            <shortDescription>
              Enter a third form of cosine of 2x.
            </shortDescription>
          </mathInput><text hide="not($answer_forms.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer
        matchPartial
        name="answer_forms"
        hide="$answer_forms.creditAchieved=1"
      >
        <award>
          <when>
            <mathList>$form_one $form_two $form_three</mathList> =
            $cos_double_angle_forms
          </when>
        </award>
      </answer>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    Using these, we can isolate either <m>\sin^2(x)</m> or <m>\cos^2(x)</m> in
    identities that eliminate powers of trigonometric functions on the other
    side. That leaves us with the two useful identities
    <ul>
      <li>
        <mathInput name="sine_squared">
          <!-- prefillLatex="\frac{1-\cos(2\cdot x)}{2}" -->
          <label><m>\sin^2(x) =</m></label>
        </mathInput><text hide="not($final_ids.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <mathInput
          name="cosine_squared"
        > <!-- prefillLatex="\frac{1+\cos(2\cdot x)}{2}" -->
          <label><m>\cos^2(x) =</m></label>
        </mathInput><text hide="not($final_ids.creditAchieved=1)">✅</text>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <answer
      numAwardsCredited="2"
      name="final_ids"
      hide="$final_ids.creditAchieved=1"
    >
      <award credit=".5">
        <when>$sine_squared=<m>\frac{1-\cos(2\cdot x)}{2}</m></when>
      </award>
      <award credit=".5">
        <when>$cosine_squared=<m>\frac{1+\cos(2\cdot x)}{2}</m></when>
      </award>
    </answer>
  </div>
  <div>
    Thus we may use the final identities for <m>\sin^2(x)</m> and
    <m>\cos^2(x)</m> to simplify the computation of integrals involving only
    even powers of sine and cosine functions.
  </div>
</cascade>